                {
                    "type": "action",
                    "name": "Steelpush: Propel",
                    "img": "icons/magic/movement/trail-streak-zigzag-yellow.webp",
                    "_id": "1XURjh3MR0RGUGIa",
                    "system": {
                        "id": "steelpush-propel",
                        "type": "metallic-arts",
                        "description": {
                            "value": "<p>While burning steel, spend 1 Investiture or more, up to your Metallic Art limit, to Steelpush a metal object you sense with this power.</p><p><strong>Propel.</strong> Either you or the object, whichever is smaller, is Steelpushed up to 20 feet per Investiture spent, moving in a straight line away from the other. If you’re the same size as the object, you choose whether to move yourself or it. If you propel an object into another sufficiently large object or surface (such as a building or the ground), the Steelpushed object ceases to move, and you’re propelled the remainder of the distance.</p><p>To move an object that’s affixed to another object, or that’s worn or held by a character, use their combined size to determine what moves.</p>",
