                {
                    "type": "action",
                    "name": "Steelpush: Shoot Coin",
                    "img": "icons/commodities/currency/coin-engraved-waves-copper.webp",
                    "_id": "Lc7ZZ1CetzaaGvYD",
                    "system": {
                        "id": "steelpush-shoot-coin",
                        "type": "metallic-arts",
                        "description": {
                            "value": "<p>While burning steel, spend 1 Investiture or more, up to your Metallic Art limit, to Steelpush a metal object you sense with this power.</p><p><strong>Shoot Coin.</strong> If the object is smaller than you, you can Steelpush it up to 20 feet per Investiture spent, shooting it with such force that it becomes a dangerous projectile. Make a ranged Allomancy attack against the Physical defense of a target within that range, rolling [[damage 1d4 Impact]]. That roll uses your Metallic Art die, so its size increases with your ranks in Allomancy; at 2 ranks, roll 1d6 instead of 1d4, and so on. (This counts as a weapon attack with a metal projectile.)</p><p>To move an object that’s affixed to another object, or that’s worn or held by a character, use their combined size to determine what moves.</p>",
